  (text "Bridgeville RTK Base -- Power Scheduler Add-On Board\nReference schematic (connections). Every part drawn as a labelled rectangle;\nsame net name on two pins = electrically connected, regardless of position on the sheet.\nDraft 2026-09-04 -- see project doc 'Bridgeville Power Scheduler - ESP32 Redesign' for rationale."
    (at 40 40 0)
    (effects (font (size 3.0 3.0)))
    (uuid 1522600d-0fb5-4ae9-a788-a7a81c880ee7)
  )
  (text "NOTES:\n- BATT_12V / GND = always-hot battery bus tap (NOT the Renogy Load terminals).\n- U3 Out-1's Aux-control pins are intentionally left disconnected (defaults ON per its\n  manual) -- Q1/Q2/R1/R2 do the actual Pi power switching instead.\n- K1 relay is single-coil latching: DRV8871 IN1=H/IN2=L sets (NO closes -> power ON),\n  IN1=L/IN2=H resets (NO opens -> power OFF); both low = idle, no coil current either way.\n- J1/J2/J3 are wiring pigtails/headers, not connector part numbers -- use what you have.\n- Verify K1 and Q1/Q2 pinouts against the physical parts' printed diagrams before wiring;\n  this schematic gives function per pin (COILA/COM/NO/... , GATE/SOURCE/DRAIN, etc.),\n  not manufacturer pin-1 markings."
    (at 40 480 0)
    (effects (font (size 2.5 2.5)))
